{"title": "Sectional Mock #109 (Mixed)", "duration_min": 30.0, "questions": [{"q_en": "<p>If X - Y = 8 and X<sup>3</sup>  -  Y<sup>3</sup> = 1304, then find the value of X<sup>4</sup> + Y<sup>4 </sup>is: </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; X - Y = 8 &#2324;&#2352; X<sup>3</sup> - Y<sup>3</sup> = 1304, &#2340;&#2379; X<sup>4</sup> + Y<sup>4</sup> &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;: </p>", "options_en": ["14722", "14920", "14836", "14638"], "options_hi": ["14722", "14920", "14836", "14638"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>X<sup>3</sup>  -  Y<sup>3</sup> = (X  -  Y) [(X  -  Y)<sup>2</sup> + 3XY] </p><p>1304 = 8 [8<sup>2</sup> + 3XY] </p><p>163 = 64 + 3XY </p><p>XY = 33</p><p>So, X = 11</p><p>Y = 3 </p><p>X<sup>4</sup> + Y<sup>4</sup> = 14641 + 81 </p><p>= 14722 </p>", "solution_hi": "<p>X<sup>3</sup>  -  Y<sup>3</sup> = (X  -  Y) [(X  -  Y)<sup>2</sup> + 3XY] </p><p>1304 = 8 [8<sup>2</sup> + 3XY] </p><p>163 = 64 + 3XY </p><p>XY = 33</p><p>So, X = 11</p><p>Y = 3 </p><p>X<sup>4</sup> + Y<sup>4</sup> = 14641 + 81 </p><p>= 14722 </p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>The length of a train is (X  -  10) m. If it is running at the speed of 64 km/hr and crosses a (X + 30) m long bridge in 18 sec, then find the value of X.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; (X - 10) m &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2351;&#2361; 64 km/hr &#2325;&#2368; &#2330;&#2366;&#2354; &#2360;&#2375; &#2330;&#2354; &#2352;&#2361;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; 18 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2319;&#2325; (X + 30) m &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2375; &#2346;&#2369;&#2354; &#2325;&#2379; &#2346;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; X &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["140", "150", "120", "160"], "options_hi": ["140", "150", "120", "160"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Speed of train = 64 km/hr = 64 * 5/18 = 160/9 m/sec</p><p>Total distance covered = X  -  10 + X + 30 = (2X + 20) m</p><p>Then,</p><p>2X + 20 = 18 * 160/9</p><p>2X + 20 = 320</p><p>2X = 300</p><p>X = 150 </p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Speed of train = 64 km/hr = 64 * 5/18 = 160/9 m/sec</p><p>Total distance covered = X  -  10 + X + 30 = (2X + 20) m</p><p>Then,</p><p>2X + 20 = 18 * 160/9</p><p>2X + 20 = 320</p><p>2X = 300</p><p>X = 150 </p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>Ankita gives Aditi a head start of 20 m in a race of 720 m. Ankita runs at a speed of 28.8 km/h. If Ankita managed to beat Aditi by 10 seconds, find the ratio of speeds of Ankita and Aditi if they started the race at the same time.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2366; 720 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2309;&#2342;&#2367;&#2340;&#2367; &#2360;&#2375; 20 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2310;&#2327;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2366; 28.8 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2360;&#2375; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2366; &#2309;&#2342;&#2367;&#2340;&#2367; &#2360;&#2375; 10 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337; &#2310;&#2327;&#2375; &#2344;&#2367;&#2325;&#2354; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; &#2309;&#2342;&#2367;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;, &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2313;&#2344;&#2381;&#2361;&#2379;&#2306;&#2344;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2361;&#2368; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2346;&#2352; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2370; &#2325;&#2368; &#2361;&#2379;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["9: 7", "8: 7", "8: 5", "6: 5"], "options_hi": ["9: 7", "8: 7", "8: 5", "6: 5"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p><b>[To convert km/h in m/s, multiply with 5/18]</b></p><p>28.8 km/h = 8 m/sec</p><p>Time taken by Ankita = 720/8 = 90 seconds</p><p>Distance covered by Aditi = 720  -  20 =700 m</p><p>Time taken by Aditi = 90 + 10 =100 seconds</p><p>The speed of Aditi = 700/100 = 7</p><p>Hence, the required ratio = 8/7</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><b>[To convert km/h in m/s, multiply with 5/18]</b></p><p>28.8 km/h = 8 m/sec</p><p>Time taken by Ankita = 720/8 = 90 seconds</p><p>Distance covered by Aditi = 720  -  20 =700 m</p><p>Time taken by Aditi = 90 + 10 =100 seconds</p><p>The speed of Aditi = 700/100 = 7</p><p>Hence, the required ratio = 8/7</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>Sum of two numbers is 144. If larger number is increased by 30% and the smaller number is decreased by 30%, then their difference become 75.2. Find 25% of the smaller number. </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327; 144 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2348;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 30% &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2325;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2331;&#2379;&#2335;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 30% &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2350;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2319;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; 75.2 &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2331;&#2379;&#2335;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; 25% &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["8", "14", "16", "19.5"], "options_hi": ["8", "14", "16", "19.5"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Let the numbers are a (larger) and b (smaller). </p><p>a + b = 144 =&gt; a = 144  -  b </p><p>And (100 + 30)% of a  -  (100  -  30)% of b = 75.2</p><p>13a  -  7b = 752 =&gt; a = (752 + 7b)/13 </p><p>Now, 144  -  b = (752 + 7b)/13</p><p>1872  -  13b = 752 + 7b </p><p>20b = 1120</p><p>b = 56</p><p>Therefore, 25% of b = 25% of 56 = <b>14</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the numbers are a (larger) and b (smaller). </p><p>a + b = 144 =&gt; a = 144  -  b </p><p>And (100 + 30)% of a  -  (100  -  30)% of b = 75.2</p><p>13a  -  7b = 752 =&gt; a = (752 + 7b)/13 </p><p>Now, 144  -  b = (752 + 7b)/13</p><p>1872  -  13b = 752 + 7b </p><p>20b = 1120</p><p>b = 56</p><p>Therefore, 25% of b = 25% of 56 = <b>14</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>If the interest is compounded Bi-annually, find the compound interest on Rs 2000 for 4 years at 10% per annum.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2367; -&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2367;&#2325; &#2340;&#2380;&#2352; &#2346;&#2352; &#2330;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2330;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, 2000 &#2352;&#2369; &#2346;&#2352; 10% &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2367;&#2325; &#2342;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2330;&#2366;&#2352; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2330;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["Rs 800", "Rs 1440", "Rs 2800", "Rs 880"], "options_hi": ["800 &#2352;&#2369;", "1440 &#2352;&#2369;", "2800 &#2352;&#2369;", "880 &#2352;&#2369;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>if the interest is compounded Bi-annually, time = 4/2=2</p> <p>rate of interest= 10*2=20</p> <p>CI = 2000[(1+(20/100))<sup>2</sup> - 1]</p> <p>CI= 2000[36/25 -1]</p> <p>CI= 2000*11/25 = Rs 880</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>if the interest is compounded Bi-annually, time = 4/2=2</p> <p>rate of interest= 10*2=20</p> <p>CI = 2000[(1+(20/100))<sup>2</sup> - 1]</p> <p>CI= 2000[36/25 -1]</p> <p>CI= 2000*11/25 = Rs 880</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}, {"q_en": "<p>The number of prime numbers between 40 to 90 is - </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2366; &#2325;&#2341;&#2344; &#2360;&#2361;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["13", "11", "12", "14"], "options_hi": ["&#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2309;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2367;&#2359;&#2350; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340;&#2367;&#2325; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;", "&#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339;&#2366;&#2306;&#2325; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;", "&#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339;&#2366;&#2306;&#2325; &#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340;&#2367;&#2325; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;", "&#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2375;&#2351; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340;&#2367;&#2325; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Prime numbers between 40 to 90 = 41, 43, 47, 53, 59, 61, 67, 71, 73, 79, 83, 89</p><p>Numbers = 12</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Prime numbers between 40 to 90 = 41, 43, 47, 53, 59, 61, 67, 71, 73, 79, 83, 89</p><p>Numbers = 12</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the total surface area of a pyramid which is based on a rectangle of length 20 cm and breadth 14 cm, and height 24 cm.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2367;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350;&#2367;&#2337; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2346;&#2371;&#2359;&#2381;&#2336;&#2368;&#2351; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319; &#2332;&#2379; 20 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312;, 14 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2330;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366;&#2312; &#2324;&#2352; 24 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2314;&#2306;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340; &#2346;&#2352; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2367;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["1144 cm<sup>2</sup>", "1430 cm<sup>2</sup>", "1830 cm<sup>2</sup>", "1550 cm<sup>2</sup>"], "options_hi": ["1144 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup>", "1430 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup>", "1830 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup>", "1550 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup>"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>[In this pyramid, two slant heights, one from the base side and the other from the length side]</p><p>Slant height (breadth) = &radic;[24<sup>2</sup> + (14/2)<sup>2</sup>] = &radic;[576 + 49] = 25 cm</p><p>Slant height (Length) = &radic;[24<sup>2</sup> + (20/2)<sup>2</sup>] = &radic;[576 + 100] = 26 cm</p><p>Lateral surface area = 2 * 1/2 * base * slant height + 2 * 1/2 * length * slant height</p><p>= 14 * 26 + 20 * 25</p><p>= 864 cm<sup>2</sup></p><p>Total surface area of pyramid = Lateral surface area + Base area</p><p>= 864 + 20 * 14</p><p>= 1144 cm<sup>2</sup></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>[In this pyramid, two slant heights, one from the base side and the other from the length side]</p><p>Slant height (breadth) = &radic;[24<sup>2</sup> + (14/2)<sup>2</sup>] = &radic;[576 + 49] = 25 cm</p><p>Slant height (Length) = &radic;[24<sup>2</sup> + (20/2)<sup>2</sup>] = &radic;[576 + 100] = 26 cm</p><p>Lateral surface area = 2 * 1/2 * base * slant height + 2 * 1/2 * length * slant height</p><p>= 14 * 26 + 20 * 25</p><p>= 864 cm<sup>2</sup></p><p>Total surface area of pyramid = Lateral surface area + Base area</p><p>= 864 + 20 * 14</p><p>= 1144 cm<sup>2</sup></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>A solid metallic cuboid of dimensions 18 cm * 25 cm * 60 cm is melted and converted into a cube whose side length is X cm. What is the lateral surface area (in sq. cm) of cube?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>18 cm * 25 cm * 60 cm &#2357;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2336;&#2379;&#2360; &#2343;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2357;&#2367;&#2325; &#2328;&#2344;&#2366;&#2349; &#2325;&#2379; &#2346;&#2367;&#2328;&#2354;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2328;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2332;&#2361;&#2366;&#2305; &#2328;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; X cm &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2328;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2381;&#2357; &#2346;&#2371;&#2359;&#2381;&#2336;&#2368;&#2351; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; (sq. cm &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["4800", "3600", "5400", "4000"], "options_hi": ["4800", "3600", "5400", "4000"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Volume of cube = Volume of cuboid</p><p>X<sup>3</sup> = 18 x 25 x 60</p><p>X<sup>3</sup> = 9 x 2 x 5 x 5 x 5 x 3 x 2 x 2</p><p>X = 3 x 2 x 5</p><p>X = 30 cm</p><p>Lateral surface area of cube = 4 * X<sup>2</sup></p><p>= 4 * 30 * 30</p><p>= 3600 sq. cm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Volume of cube = Volume of cuboid</p><p>X<sup>3</sup> = 18 x 25 x 60</p><p>X<sup>3</sup> = 9 x 2 x 5 x 5 x 5 x 3 x 2 x 2</p><p>X = 3 x 2 x 5</p><p>X = 30 cm</p><p>Lateral surface area of cube = 4 * X<sup>2</sup></p><p>= 4 * 30 * 30</p><p>= 3600 sq. cm</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (3D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>If 81a<sup>4</sup> + 225a<sup>2</sup>b<sup>2</sup> + 625b<sup>4</sup> = 882 and 9a<sup>2</sup> + 25b<sup>2</sup>  -  15ab = 21, then what is the value of 6ab? </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 81a<sup>4</sup> + 225a<sup>2</sup>b<sup>2</sup> + 625b<sup>4</sup> = 882 &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; 9a<sup>2</sup> + 25b<sup>2</sup> - 15ab = 21, &#2340;&#2379; 6ab &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["21/2", "21/4", "21/5", "7/2"], "options_hi": ["21/2", "21/4", "21/5", "7/2"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>9a<sup>2</sup> + 25b<sup>2</sup>  -  15ab = 21 ... (i)</p><p>81a<sup>4</sup> + 225a<sup>2</sup>b<sup>2</sup> + 625b<sup>4</sup> = 882 </p><p>(9a<sup>2</sup>)<sup>2</sup> + 9a<sup>2 </sup>* 25b<sup>2</sup> + (25b<sup>2</sup>)<sup>2</sup> = 882 </p><p>(9a<sup>2</sup> + 15ab + 25b<sup>2</sup>) (9a<sup>2</sup>  -  15ab + 25b<sup>2</sup>) = 882 </p><p>(9a<sup>2</sup> + 15ab + 25b<sup>2</sup>) * 21 = 882 </p><p>9a<sup>2</sup> + 15ab + 25b<sup>2</sup> = 42 ... (ii)</p><p>Subtract (i) from (ii) </p><p>30ab = 21 </p><p>6ab = 21/5 </p>", "solution_hi": "<p>9a<sup>2</sup> + 25b<sup>2</sup>  -  15ab = 21 ... (i)</p><p>81a<sup>4</sup> + 225a<sup>2</sup>b<sup>2</sup> + 625b<sup>4</sup> = 882 </p><p>(9a<sup>2</sup>)<sup>2</sup> + 9a<sup>2 </sup>* 25b<sup>2</sup> + (25b<sup>2</sup>)<sup>2</sup> = 882 </p><p>(9a<sup>2</sup> + 15ab + 25b<sup>2</sup>) (9a<sup>2</sup>  -  15ab + 25b<sup>2</sup>) = 882 </p><p>(9a<sup>2</sup> + 15ab + 25b<sup>2</sup>) * 21 = 882 </p><p>9a<sup>2</sup> + 15ab + 25b<sup>2</sup> = 42 ... (ii)</p><p>Subtract (i) from (ii) </p><p>30ab = 21 </p><p>6ab = 21/5 </p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>Shane borrows &#8377;30,000 from a bank at a simple interest rate of 10% per annum for 3 years. However, he is unable to repay the loan on time and requests an extension of 3 more years. The bank adds the interest from the first 3 years to the principal for the next 3 years at the same interest rate. What is the total amount Shane pays at the end of 6 years?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2358;&#2375;&#2344; &#2344;&#2375; 3 &#2360;&#2366;&#2354; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; 10% &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2366;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2339; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2342;&#2352; &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2376;&#2306;&#2325; &#2360;&#2375; 30,000 &#2337;&#2377;&#2354;&#2352; &#2313;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404; &#2361;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366;&#2305;&#2325;&#2367;, &#2357;&#2361; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2346;&#2352; &#2315;&#2339; &#2330;&#2369;&#2325;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2309;&#2360;&#2350;&#2352;&#2381;&#2341; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; 3 &#2324;&#2352; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2357;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2352;&#2379;&#2343; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2348;&#2376;&#2306;&#2325; &#2346;&#2361;&#2354;&#2375; 3 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2325;&#2379; &#2309;&#2327;&#2354;&#2375; 3 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2313;&#2360;&#2368; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2342;&#2352; &#2346;&#2352; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2343;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2332;&#2379;&#2337;&#2364;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; 6 &#2360;&#2366;&#2354; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2358;&#2375;&#2344; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2330;&#2369;&#2325;&#2366;&#2312; &#2327;&#2312; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["50700", "50300", "49200", "51300"], "options_hi": ["50700", "50300", "49200", "51300"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Simple interest in 3 years = 30000 x 10 x 3/100 = Rs.9000</p><p>New Principal for next 3 years = 30000 + 9000 = Rs.39000</p><p>Total amount paid at the end of 6 years = 39000 + (39000 x 10 x 3/100)</p><p>= 39000 + 11700</p><p>= Rs.50700</p><p></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Simple interest in 3 years = 30000 x 10 x 3/100 = Rs.9000</p><p>New Principal for next 3 years = 30000 + 9000 = Rs.39000</p><p>Total amount paid at the end of 6 years = 39000 + (39000 x 10 x 3/100)</p><p>= 39000 + 11700</p><p>= Rs.50700</p><p></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}, {"q_en": "<p>Three stacks of notebooks contain 288, 432, and 576 notebooks. The notebooks are to be arranged in equal-sized piles. What is the largest number of notebooks per pile, and how many piles will be there in total?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2379;&#2335;&#2348;&#2369;&#2325; &#2325;&#2375; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2338;&#2375;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 288, 432 &#2324;&#2352; 576 &#2344;&#2379;&#2335;&#2348;&#2369;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2311;&#2344; &#2344;&#2379;&#2335;&#2348;&#2369;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2310;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2338;&#2375;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2338;&#2375;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2344;&#2379;&#2335;&#2348;&#2369;&#2325; &#2325;&#2368; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2338;&#2375;&#2352; &#2361;&#2379;&#2306;&#2327;&#2375;?</p>", "options_en": ["15 piles", "9 piles", "11 piles", "13 piles"], "options_hi": ["15 &#2338;&#2375;&#2352;", "9 &#2338;&#2375;&#2352;", "11 &#2338;&#2375;&#2352;", "13 &#2338;&#2375;&#2352;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Factor of 288 = 2<sup>5</sup> * 3<sup>2</sup></p><p>Factor of 432 = 2<sup>4 </sup>* 3<sup>3</sup></p><p>Factor of 576 = 2<sup>6</sup> * 3<sup>2</sup></p><p>HCF = 2<sup>4</sup> * 3<sup>2</sup> = 16 * 9 = 144</p><p>288/144 = 2 piles</p><p>432/144 = 3 piles</p><p>576/144 = 4 piles</p><p>Total number of piles = 2 + 3 + 4 = 9 piles</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Factor of 288 = 2<sup>5</sup> * 3<sup>2</sup></p><p>Factor of 432 = 2<sup>4 </sup>* 3<sup>3</sup></p><p>Factor of 576 = 2<sup>6</sup> * 3<sup>2</sup></p><p>HCF = 2<sup>4</sup> * 3<sup>2</sup> = 16 * 9 = 144</p><p>288/144 = 2 piles</p><p>432/144 = 3 piles</p><p>576/144 = 4 piles</p><p>Total number of piles = 2 + 3 + 4 = 9 piles</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>A boat takes the same time to travel 18 km upstream as to travel 24 km downstream. What is the ratio of its speed in still water to the speed of the stream?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2366;&#2357; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; 18 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368; &#2330;&#2354;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2313;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2368; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2354;&#2375;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2332;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; 24 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368; &#2330;&#2354;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2375;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2352; &#2332;&#2354; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2324;&#2352; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["6 : 1", "7 : 1", "8 : 1", "9 : 1"], "options_hi": ["6 : 1", "7 : 1", "8 : 1", "9 : 1"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Let, speed of boat in still water and speed of stream be b km/h and s km/h respectively.</p><p>18/(b  -  s) = 24/(b + s) =&gt; 18(b + s) = 24(b  -  s)</p><p>=&gt; 18b + 18s = 24b  -  24s =&gt; 42s = 6b =&gt; b/s = 42/6 = 7/1</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let, speed of boat in still water and speed of stream be b km/h and s km/h respectively.</p><p>18/(b  -  s) = 24/(b + s) =&gt; 18(b + s) = 24(b  -  s)</p><p>=&gt; 18b + 18s = 24b  -  24s =&gt; 42s = 6b =&gt; b/s = 42/6 = 7/1</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p><div>&nbsp;If&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">x", "q_hi": "<p><div>&nbsp;&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">x", "options_en": ["110", "130", "160", "180"], "options_hi": ["110", "130", "160", "180"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>If x/(x&#178; - 2x + 1) = 1/3, then find the value of x&ge; + 1/x&ge;.</p><p>Recognize that x&#178; - 2x + 1 = (x - 1)&#178;. The equation becomes:</p><p>&#8195;&#8195;x/(x - 1)&#178; = 1/3.</p><p>Multiply both sides by (x - 1)&#178;:</p><p>&#8195;&#8195;x = (x - 1)&#178;/3.</p><p>&#8195;&#8195;Then multiply by 3:</p><p>&#8195;&#8195;3x = (x - 1)&#178;.</p><p>Expand (x - 1)&#178;:</p><p>&#8195;&#8195;3x = x&#178; - 2x + 1.</p><p>&#8195;&#8195;Rearrange to form a quadratic:</p><p>&#8195;&#8195;x&#178; - 5x + 1 = 0.</p><p>Divide the quadratic by x (x &#8800; 0):</p><p>&#8195;&#8195;x - 5 + 1/x = 0, which gives:</p><p>&#8195;&#8195;x + 1/x = 5.</p><p>Use the identity:</p><p>&#8195;&#8195;(x + 1/x)&ge; = x&ge; + 1/x&ge; + 3(x + 1/x).</p><p>&#8195;&#8195;Substitute x + 1/x = 5:</p><p>&#8195;&#8195;125 = x&ge; + 1/x&ge; + 15.</p><p>&#8195;&#8195;Thus, x&ge; + 1/x&ge; = 125 - 15 = 110.</p><p>Option (a) is the correct answer.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>If x/(x&#178; - 2x + 1) = 1/3, then find the value of x&ge; + 1/x&ge;.</p><p>Recognize that x&#178; - 2x + 1 = (x - 1)&#178;. The equation becomes:</p><p>&#8195;&#8195;x/(x - 1)&#178; = 1/3.</p><p>Multiply both sides by (x - 1)&#178;:</p><p>&#8195;&#8195;x = (x - 1)&#178;/3.</p><p>&#8195;&#8195;Then multiply by 3:</p><p>&#8195;&#8195;3x = (x - 1)&#178;.</p><p>Expand (x - 1)&#178;:</p><p>&#8195;&#8195;3x = x&#178; - 2x + 1.</p><p>&#8195;&#8195;Rearrange to form a quadratic:</p><p>&#8195;&#8195;x&#178; - 5x + 1 = 0.</p><p>Divide the quadratic by x (x &#8800; 0):</p><p>&#8195;&#8195;x - 5 + 1/x = 0, which gives:</p><p>&#8195;&#8195;x + 1/x = 5.</p><p>Use the identity:</p><p>&#8195;&#8195;(x + 1/x)&ge; = x&ge; + 1/x&ge; + 3(x + 1/x).</p><p>&#8195;&#8195;Substitute x + 1/x = 5:</p><p>&#8195;&#8195;125 = x&ge; + 1/x&ge; + 15.</p><p>&#8195;&#8195;Thus, x&ge; + 1/x&ge; = 125 - 15 = 110.</p><p>Option (a) is the correct answer.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>A rectangular sheet of metal is 55 cm by 35 cm. Equal squares of side 5 cm are cut off at the corners and the remainder is folded up to form an open rectangular box. Find the volume of the box.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2343;&#2366;&#2340;&#2369; &#2325;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2358;&#2368;&#2335; 55 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2327;&#2369;&#2339;&#2366; 35 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; 5 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2346;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366;&#2335;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359; &#2325;&#2379; &#2350;&#2379;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2326;&#2369;&#2354;&#2366; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2348;&#2377;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360; &#2348;&#2344;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2348;&#2377;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360; &#2325;&#2366; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["5625 cm<sup>3</sup>", "5525 cm<sup>3</sup>", "5475 cm<sup>3</sup>", "5595 cm<sup>3</sup>"], "options_hi": ["5625 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>3</sup>", "5525 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>3</sup>", "5475 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>3</sup>", "5595 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>3</sup>"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>New Length of the box = 55 - 2 x 5 = 45 cm</p><p>New width of the box = 35 - 2 x 5 = 25 cm</p><p>Height of the box = 5 cm</p><p>Volume of the box = 45 x 25 x 5 = 5625 cm<sup>3</sup></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>New Length of the box = 55 - 2 x 5 = 45 cm</p><p>New width of the box = 35 - 2 x 5 = 25 cm</p><p>Height of the box = 5 cm</p><p>Volume of the box = 45 x 25 x 5 = 5625 cm<sup>3</sup></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (3D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>Read the following data carefully and answer the following questions. The following table shows the total number of students (boys + girls) in four different classes and the total number of boys in four different classes. </p><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;\"><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\"></td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\"><b>The total number of students (boys + girls)</b></td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\"><b>The total number of boys </b></td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\"><b>Class V</b></td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">600</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">375</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\"><b>Class VI</b></td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">800</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">450</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\"><b>Class VII</b></td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">775</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">325</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\"><b>Class VIII</b></td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">550</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">275</td></tr></table><p>Find the total number of girls in classes VI, VIII, and V together. </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2310;&#2305;&#2325;&#2396;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2343;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2344;&#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2357;&#2325; &#2346;&#2338;&#2364;&#2375;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2358;&#2381;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2352; &#2342;&#2375;&#2306;&#2404; &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2340;&#2366;&#2354;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366; &#2330;&#2366;&#2352; &#2309;&#2354;&#2327;-&#2309;&#2354;&#2327; &#2325;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2331;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; (&#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2375; + &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306;) &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2330;&#2366;&#2352; &#2309;&#2354;&#2327;-&#2309;&#2354;&#2327; &#2325;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;\"><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\"></td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\"><b>&#2331;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; (&#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2375;+&#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2305;)</b></td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\"><b>&#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;</b></td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\"><b>&#2325;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366; V</b></td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">600</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">375</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\"><b>&#2325;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366; VI</b></td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">800</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">450</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\"><b>&#2325;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366; VII</b></td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">775</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">325</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\"><b>&#2325;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366; VIII</b></td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">550</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">275</td></tr></table><p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2325;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366; VI, VIII &#2324;&#2352; V &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2351;&#2375;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["850", "875", "800", "825"], "options_hi": ["850", "875", "800", "825"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>The total number of girls in class VI = 800  -  450 = 350 </p><p>The total number of girls in class VIII = 550  -  275 = 275 </p><p>The total number of girls in class V = 600  -  375 = 225 </p><p>Hence, the required value = 350 + 275 + 225 = 850 </p>", "solution_hi": "<p>The total number of girls in class VI = 800  -  450 = 350 </p><p>The total number of girls in class VIII = 550  -  275 = 275 </p><p>The total number of girls in class V = 600  -  375 = 225 </p><p>Hence, the required value = 350 + 275 + 225 = 850 </p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>The side of an equilateral triangle is 12 cm. What is the area (in cm<sup>2</sup>, rounded off to 2 decimal places) of the triangle? Given: &radic;3 = 1.732</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2348;&#2366;&#2361;&#2369; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; 12 cm &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; (cm<sup>2 </sup>&#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#2342;&#2358;&#2350;&#2354;&#2357; &#2325;&#2375; 2 &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2340;&#2325; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339;&#2366;&#2306;&#2325;&#2367;&#2340;) &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;? &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;: &radic;3 = 1.732</p>", "options_en": ["68.07", "63.89", "62.35", "65.23"], "options_hi": ["68.07", "63.89", "62.35", "65.23"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Area of an equilateral triangle of side 'a' = &radic;3a<sup>2</sup>/4</p><p>= 1.732 * 12<sup>2</sup>/4</p><p>= 1.732 * 36</p><p>= 62.352</p><p>= 62.35 cm<sup>2</sup></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Area of an equilateral triangle of side 'a' = &radic;3a<sup>2</sup>/4</p><p>= 1.732 * 12<sup>2</sup>/4</p><p>= 1.732 * 36</p><p>= 62.352</p><p>= 62.35 cm<sup>2</sup></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>Calculate the difference between the compound interest and the simple interest on a sum of &#8377;5,000 at the rate of 8% for 3 years. (to nearest &#8377;)</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#8377;5,000 &#2325;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2346;&#2352; 8% &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; 3 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2330;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2324;&#2352; &#2360;&#2366;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2339; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2339;&#2344;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404; (&#2344;&#2367;&#2325;&#2335;&#2340;&#2350; &#8377; &#2340;&#2325;)</p>", "options_en": ["&#8377;108", "&#8377;105", "&#8377;102", "&#8377;99"], "options_hi": ["&#8377;108", "&#8377;105", "&#8377;102", "&#8377;99"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>P = 5000 Rs., R = 8%, T = 3 years</p><p>Simple interest = 5000 * 8 * 3/100 = 1200 Rs.</p><p>Compound interest = 5000[(1 + 8/100)<sup>3</sup>  -  1]</p><p>= 5000 *(19683  - 15625)/15625</p><p>= 5000 * 4058/15625</p><p>= 1298.56&#8776; 1299 Rs.</p><p>Required difference = 1299  -  1200 = 99 Rs.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>P = 5000 Rs., R = 8%, T = 3 years</p><p>Simple interest = 5000 * 8 * 3/100 = 1200 Rs.</p><p>Compound interest = 5000[(1 + 8/100)<sup>3</sup>  -  1]</p><p>= 5000 *(19683  - 15625)/15625</p><p>= 5000 * 4058/15625</p><p>= 1298.56&#8776; 1299 Rs.</p><p>Required difference = 1299  -  1200 = 99 Rs.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}, {"q_en": "<p>The ratio of number of students who attended the whole seminar to that who attended the seminar in beginning from college T is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2360;&#2350;&#2381;&#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2366;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2366;&#2327; &#2354;&#2375;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2342;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; &#2350;&#2361;&#2366;&#2357;&#2367;&#2342;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2354;&#2351; T &#2360;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2352;&#2306;&#2349; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2366;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2366;&#2327; &#2354;&#2375;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2342;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376;:</p>", "options_en": ["25: 36", "5: 72", "25: 72", "5: 36"], "options_hi": ["25: 36", "5: 72", "25: 72", "5: 36"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Number of students who attended the whole seminar from college T = 5000 * 10/100 = 500</p><p>Number of students who attended the seminar in beginning from college T = 7200 * 20/100 = 1440</p><p>Required ratio = 500: 1440 = 25: 72</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Number of students who attended the whole seminar from college T = 5000 * 10/100 = 500</p><p>Number of students who attended the seminar in beginning from college T = 7200 * 20/100 = 1440</p><p>Required ratio = 500: 1440 = 25: 72</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>If (3x + y + 4z) = 12 and 3xy + 4yz + 12zx = 26, then the value of (9x<sup>2</sup> + y<sup>2</sup> + 16z<sup>2</sup>) is equal to:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; (3x + y + 4z) = 12 &#2324;&#2352; 3xy + 4yz + 12zx = 26 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; (9x<sup>2</sup> + y<sup>2</sup> + 16z<sup>2</sup>) &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;:</p>", "options_en": ["78", "88", "92", "34"], "options_hi": ["78", "88", "92", "34"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Given, (3x + y + 4z) = 12 and 3xy + 4yz + 12zx = 26,</p><p>We know that,</p><p>(a + b + c)<sup>2</sup> = a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> + c<sup>2</sup> + 2ab + 2bc + 2ca</p><p>(3x + y + 4z) = 12</p><p>=&gt; (3x + y + 4z)<sup>2</sup> = 144</p><p>=&gt; 9x<sup>2</sup> + y<sup>2</sup> + 16z<sup>2</sup> + 6xy + 8yz + 24zx = 144</p><p>=&gt; 9x<sup>2</sup> + y<sup>2</sup> + 16z<sup>2</sup> + 2 * 26 = 144</p><p>=&gt; 9x<sup>2</sup> + y<sup>2</sup> + 16z<sup>2</sup> = 144  -  52 = 92</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Given, (3x + y + 4z) = 12 and 3xy + 4yz + 12zx = 26,</p><p>We know that,</p><p>(a + b + c)<sup>2</sup> = a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> + c<sup>2</sup> + 2ab + 2bc + 2ca</p><p>(3x + y + 4z) = 12</p><p>=&gt; (3x + y + 4z)<sup>2</sup> = 144</p><p>=&gt; 9x<sup>2</sup> + y<sup>2</sup> + 16z<sup>2</sup> + 6xy + 8yz + 24zx = 144</p><p>=&gt; 9x<sup>2</sup> + y<sup>2</sup> + 16z<sup>2</sup> + 2 * 26 = 144</p><p>=&gt; 9x<sup>2</sup> + y<sup>2</sup> + 16z<sup>2</sup> = 144  -  52 = 92</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>Which of the following numbers does not lie between 21/28 and 32/36?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2358; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 110% &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2325;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2361;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 16% &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2350;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2339;&#2366;&#2350;&#2368; &#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; 4/3 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354; &#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["16/21", "15/19", "14/18", "18/25"], "options_hi": ["2/3", "3/8", "5/9", "8/15"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>21/28 = 0.75, 32/36 = 0.88</p><p>(a) 16/21 = 0.76, 0.88 &gt; 0.76 &gt; 0.75</p><p>(b) 15/19 = 0.78, 0.88 &gt; 0.78 &gt; 0.75</p><p>(c) 14/18 = 0.77, 0.88 &gt; 0.77 &gt; 0.75</p><p>(d) 18/25 = 0.72, 0.88 &gt; 0.72 &lt; 0.75</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>21/28 = 0.75, 32/36 = 0.88</p><p>(a) 16/21 = 0.76, 0.88 &gt; 0.76 &gt; 0.75</p><p>(b) 15/19 = 0.78, 0.88 &gt; 0.78 &gt; 0.75</p><p>(c) 14/18 = 0.77, 0.88 &gt; 0.77 &gt; 0.75</p><p>(d) 18/25 = 0.72, 0.88 &gt; 0.72 &lt; 0.75</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the volume of the pyramid, which is based on a square of side 36 cm &amp; the lateral edge of the pyramid is 30 cm.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2346;&#2367;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350;&#2367;&#2337; &#2325;&#2366; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;, &#2332;&#2379; 36 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2346;&#2352; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2367;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2367;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350;&#2367;&#2337; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2381;&#2357; &#2325;&#2367;&#2344;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; 30 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["3592&radic;3 cm<sup>3</sup>", "4296&radic;7 cm<sup>3</sup>", "2592&radic;7 cm<sup>3</sup>", "4296&radic;3 cm<sup>3</sup>"], "options_hi": ["3592&radic;3 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>3</sup>", "4296&radic;7 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>3</sup>", "2592&radic;7 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>3</sup>", "4296&radic;3 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>3</sup>"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Diagonal = side&radic;2 = 36&radic;2 cm</p><p>Height = &radic;[lateral edge<sup>2</sup>  -  (diagonal/2)<sup>2</sup>]</p><p>= &radic;(30<sup>2</sup>  -  36&radic;2/2)</p><p>= 6&radic;7 cm</p><p>The volume of the pyramid = 1/3 * (area of base) * Height</p><p>= 1/3 * (36 * 36) * 6&radic;7</p><p>= 2592&radic;7 cm<sup>3</sup></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Diagonal = side&radic;2 = 36&radic;2 cm</p><p>Height = &radic;[lateral edge<sup>2</sup>  -  (diagonal/2)<sup>2</sup>]</p><p>= &radic;(30<sup>2</sup>  -  36&radic;2/2)</p><p>= 6&radic;7 cm</p><p>The volume of the pyramid = 1/3 * (area of base) * Height</p><p>= 1/3 * (36 * 36) * 6&radic;7</p><p>= 2592&radic;7 cm<sup>3</sup></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>In a 1500 m race, Anil beats Bakul by 150 m and in the same race Bakul beats Charles by 75 m. By what distance does Anil beat Charles?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>1500 m &#2325;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#2309;&#2344;&#2367;&#2354; &#2344;&#2375; &#2348;&#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2325;&#2379; 150 m &#2360;&#2375; &#2361;&#2352;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2344;&#2375; &#2330;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2354;&#2381;&#2360; &#2325;&#2379; 75 m &#2360;&#2375; &#2361;&#2352;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; &#2309;&#2344;&#2367;&#2354; &#2344;&#2375; &#2330;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2354;&#2381;&#2360; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2360;&#2375; &#2361;&#2352;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["217.50 m", "200.15 m", "293.50 m", "313.75 m"], "options_hi": ["217.50 m", "200.15 m", "293.50 m", "313.75 m"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Since, Anil beats Bakul by 150 m. Which means when Anil complete 1500 m, Bakul completed only 1350 m.</p><p>Also, Bakul beats Charles by 75 m. Which means when Bakul complete 1500 m, Charles completed only 1425 m.</p><p>Total distance covered by Charles when Bakul completes only 1350 m = 1425 * (1350/1500) = 1282.5 m</p><p>Hence, the distance by which Anil beats Charles = 1500  -  1282.5</p><p>= 217.5 m</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Since, Anil beats Bakul by 150 m. Which means when Anil complete 1500 m, Bakul completed only 1350 m.</p><p>Also, Bakul beats Charles by 75 m. Which means when Bakul complete 1500 m, Charles completed only 1425 m.</p><p>Total distance covered by Charles when Bakul completes only 1350 m = 1425 * (1350/1500) = 1282.5 m</p><p>Hence, the distance by which Anil beats Charles = 1500  -  1282.5</p><p>= 217.5 m</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>Area of base of cone is 64&#960; cm<sup>2</sup> and length of slant height of the cone is 14 cm. Find the lateral surface area of the cone.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2358;&#2306;&#2325;&#2369; &#2325;&#2375; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; 64&#960; cm<sup>2 </sup>&#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2358;&#2306;&#2325;&#2369; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2367;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325; &#2314;&#2305;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; 14 cm &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2358;&#2306;&#2325;&#2369; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2381;&#2357; &#2346;&#2371;&#2359;&#2381;&#2336;&#2368;&#2351; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["374 cm<sup>2</sup>", "275 cm<sup>2</sup>", "253 cm<sup>2</sup>", "352 cm<sup>2</sup>"], "options_hi": ["374 cm<sup>2</sup>", "275 cm<sup>2</sup>", "253 cm<sup>2</sup>", "352 cm<sup>2</sup>"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Let radius of base of cone = 'r' cm</p><p>Area of base = &#960;r<sup>2</sup></p><p>64&#960; = &#960;r<sup>2</sup></p><p>r = 8 cm</p><p>Slant height = l = 14 cm</p><p>Lateral surface area of cone = &#960;rl</p><p>= (22/7) * 8 * 14</p><p>= 352 cm<sup>2</sup></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let radius of base of cone = 'r' cm</p><p>Area of base = &#960;r<sup>2</sup></p><p>64&#960; = &#960;r<sup>2</sup></p><p>r = 8 cm</p><p>Slant height = l = 14 cm</p><p>Lateral surface area of cone = &#960;rl</p><p>= (22/7) * 8 * 14</p><p>= 352 cm<sup>2</sup></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (3D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>The length, breadth, height of an ice box is 4m, 2m 40 cm, and 1 m 20 cm respectively. Find the longest rope which can measure the dimensions of the box exactly.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2310;&#2311;&#2360; &#2348;&#2377;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312;, &#2330;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366;&#2312;, &#2314;&#2305;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 4 m, 2 m 40 cm &#2324;&#2352; 1 m 20 cm &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2348;&#2377;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360; &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2335;&#2368;&#2325; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2360;&#2375; &#2350;&#2366;&#2346; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2350; &#2360;&#2348;&#2360;&#2375; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2368; &#2352;&#2360;&#2381;&#2360;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2346; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["60 cm", "50 cm", "30 cm", "40 cm"], "options_hi": ["60 cm", "50 cm", "30 cm", "40 cm"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Length = 4 m = 400 cm</p><p>Breadth = 2 m 40 cm = 240 cm</p><p>Height = 1 m 20 cm = 120 cm</p><p>Length of rope = HCF of 400, 240, and 120 = 40 cm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Length = 4 m = 400 cm</p><p>Breadth = 2 m 40 cm = 240 cm</p><p>Height = 1 m 20 cm = 120 cm</p><p>Length of rope = HCF of 400, 240, and 120 = 40 cm</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (3D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>A train is 640 m long and is running at 72 kmph. Train crosses a pole in X seconds. Find the value of X</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2352;&#2375;&#2354;&#2327;&#2366;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; 640 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; 72 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2360;&#2375; &#2330;&#2354; &#2352;&#2361;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2352;&#2375;&#2354;&#2327;&#2366;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2326;&#2306;&#2349;&#2375; &#2325;&#2379; X &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; X &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;</p>", "options_en": ["18", "16", "32", "28"], "options_hi": ["18", "16", "32", "28"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Speed of train = 72 kmph = 72 x 5/18 = 20 m/sec</p><p>Length of train = 640 m</p><p>So, X = 640/20 = 32 sec</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Speed of train = 72 kmph = 72 x 5/18 = 20 m/sec</p><p>Length of train = 640 m</p><p>So, X = 640/20 = 32 sec</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}]}